# Roles & Permissions (from PRD)

## Authorization principles
- DEFAULT DENY. Grant only what is listed here.
- Enforce at the OBJECT level, not just the view level.
- All permission checks run AFTER tenant scoping (see multi-tenancy rule): a role's
  permissions only ever apply within the user's own community (except Admin + System).
- "Registered user" = any authenticated account (Member OR Non-Member).
- **Product ACL = `User.role` + DRF permission classes** (`apps.accounts.permissions` /
  `role_checks`). Do **not** use Django Groups / `user_permissions` for product access.
- **Superadmin** = Django `is_superuser` (alias `User.is_superadmin`). Only superadmin
  has full Django `/admin` and model permissions. Changing `User.role` must go through
  `apply_user_role()` so non-superusers lose `is_staff` and Django perms.

## Role hierarchy (access level per PRD)
| Role | Platform | Level |
|------|----------|-------|
| Superadmin (`is_superuser`) | Django /admin + all product gates | Everything |
| Admin | Web dashboard | Full |
| City Founder | Web dashboard + Mobile | High |
| Team Member (Public Speaker / Content Creator) | Web dashboard | Read-only subset |
| Member | Mobile | Medium |
| Non-Member | Mobile | Low |
| Partner | Partner-side tool | Scoped (QR verify only) |
| System | Automated (Celery/services) | Internal, cross-tenant |

---

## Admin — full control across ALL countries/cities (crosses tenants)
- Approve/reject City Founder applications.
- City Founders: view all, view full profile, add manually, edit any field,
  deactivate, delete. (FR 133–137)
- Users: view all (Members + Non-Members), search/filter/sort by country/city/
  subscription/registration date, edit, deactivate, delete. (FR 138–140)
- Membership: review pending non-expat applications, approve/reject, notify. (FR 148)
- Events: view all, edit any, delete any. (FR 141–142)
- Content: view/moderate all posts + comments, remove any post/comment/media. (FR 143–145)
- Media: view all City Founder media (filterable), delete any. (FR 146–147)
- Partners/Guidebook: view/add/edit/delete. (FR 149)
- Store (MVP2): view all listings, search/filter, remove listings, view offer
  activity per listing. (FR 84, 154–156, 73)
- Trust: view each founder's score + vote count + per-event breakdown; flag/
  investigate >20pt drops; review trust comments (Admin-only, never public). (FR 125–126, 128)
- Analytics: KPIs, filter by country/city/date/user-type, view trends, export Excel. (FR 150–153)
- Account security: 2FA required; every admin action written to immutable audit log. (FR 131–132)

## City Founder — manages ONE community (tenant-scoped)
Gains access only after Admin approval of application. (FR 105)
- Events: create, edit, delete OWN community's events. (FR 160–162)
  - EDIT RESTRICTION: cannot edit ticket price or location after creation. (FR 161)
- Join requests: accept/reject Non-Member join requests for own events. (FR 167)
- Event ops: view own events w/ status, attendee lists, per-event nationality
  breakdown (used to accept/reject attendees). (FR 165–166, 169, 183)
- Team: view/add/edit/delete team members (Public Speaker / Content Creator / Other).
  System enforces minimum ≥2 speakers + ≥1 content creator; block deletions that
  breach it. (FR 170–174)
- Partners/Guidebook: add/edit/delete own partner entries. (FR 157–158)
- Media Area: upload/manage/delete photos + videos; optionally publish to feed. (FR 175–180)
- Revenue: view earnings + revenue split (ticket sales, Member vs Non-Member,
  commission), community stats. (FR 114, 181–182)
- Trust: sees OWN aggregate score only — NEVER individual voter identities. (FR 124, 127)
- Profile: "City Founder of [City]" label. (FR 103)
- Also has full Member-level social abilities on mobile (post/like/comment). (actor def)
- PUBLISH GATE (system-enforced before any event can be published): ≥10 active
  partners, ≥2 speakers, ≥1 content creator, 3 events/month commitment. (FR 159 + eligibility table)

## Team Member (Public Speaker / Content Creator) — read-only subset
- Log in to the City Founder Dashboard with own credentials. (FR 184)
- Read-only access to sections relevant to their role (e.g., event details/attendees). (FR 185)
- MUST NOT access: financial/revenue data, partner management, team management,
  event creation/deletion, or join-request approvals. Only the City Founder account
  holder has full dashboard access. (FR 185)

## Member — paid subscriber (tenant-scoped, mobile)
- Active paid subscription (monthly/annual). (FR 107)
- Events: join/purchase tickets INSTANTLY, no prior approval. (FR 41)
- Membership QR code in profile; used by partners to verify + grant discounts. (FR 51, 97)
- Discounts: redeem partner discounts via own QR (Active Member only). (Flow A, FR 54)
- Gatherings: create if attended ≥1 event; join if attended ≥1 event; max 20 attendees. (FR 22, 31, 37)
- Social: create posts (≤5 images), like, comment, view activity history, follow/
  connect. (FR 20, 26–30, 94–96, 100)
- Property (MVP2): list/edit/delete own property; browse/contact. (FR 58–62)
- Store (MVP2): list UNLIMITED products, edit/delete own, make/accept/counter/decline
  offers, buy. (FR 64–65, 71, 74, 77–78)

## Non-Member — registered, unsubscribed (tenant-scoped, mobile)
- Browse home/events/posts/partner listings; like + comment. (FR 18–20, 48)
- Events: must submit join request requiring City Founder approval; pay only after
  approval. (FR 42)
- Discounts: CANNOT redeem; can view Guidebook but NOT use QR verification flow. (FR 57)
- Gatherings: create if attended ≥3 events; join if attended ≥3 events; max 20. (FR 23, 32, 38)
- Chat with other users (MVP2 — chat deferred). (actor def)
- Property (MVP2): browse + rent/contact. (actor def)
- Store (MVP2): list MAX 1 active product (2nd prompts subscribe), buy, make offers. (FR 66, 74)
- Social: post/like/comment. (actor def)

## Partner — external, scoped (MVP1)
- ONLY capability: use the partner-side tool to scan/check a Member's QR code to
  verify active membership before granting a discount. (FR 53)
- No app account access beyond this verification flow.

## System — automated actions (internal, cross-tenant via all_tenants escape hatch)
- Membership: auto-approve expat members without admin review; route non-expat to
  pending; notify applicant of instant vs pending + ETA. (FR 9–11)
- QR: generate signed ticket QR (user_id + event_id + tamper-proof token); validate
  membership/ticket QR server-side ONLY; return member/non-member result. (FR 45, 47, 52, 54–55)
- Delivery: send tickets/invitations via WhatsApp + email + in-app ≤60s. (FR 43, 46, 168)
- Logging: log discount redemptions (timestamp/user/partner). (FR 56)
- Gatherings: reject joins once cap of 20 reached; hide location until joined. (FR 34–35)
- Subscriptions: handle renewal/expiry/cancellation, pre-expiry + expiry notices,
  1-week grace then revoke. (FR 109, 111–113)
- Trust: compute weighted-moving-average score at window close; persist score +
  cumulative count; keep voter identities hidden. (FR 121–123, 127)
- Notifications: push on likes/comments/messages/offers/event changes. (FR 29, 72, 163–164)

